","When \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) gas is passed into a mixture of \( \text{Na}^{2+}, \text{Ni}^{2+}, \text{Cl}^{2+}, \) and \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) ions in an acidified aqueous solution, the following occurs:

1. **H₂\text{S} (g) + \(\text{H}_2\text{O}\) (l) \(\rightleftharpoons\) \(\text{H}_3\text{O}^-\) (aq) + \(\text{H}_3\text{PO}_2\) (aq)**
2. **\(\text{H}_3\text{PO}_2}\) (aq) →\(\text{H}_2\text{S}\) (g) + \(\text{H}_3\text{PO}_2\) (aq)

The H₂\text{S} gas dissociates in water to form \( \text{H}_2\text{S}\) and \( \text{H}_3\text{PO}_2\). The dissociation products react with the ions in the solution to form salts.

The equilibrium constants for the formation of salts are:
\[
\text{Mn}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{MnH}_2\text{S}_3 \quad \text{(white)}
\]
\[
\text{Ni}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{NiH}_2\text{S}_3 \quad \text{(white)}
\]
\[
\text{Cl}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{ClH}_2\text{S}_3 \quad \text{(white)}
\]
\[
\text{Hg}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{HgH}_2\text{S}_3 \quad \text{(white)}
\]

The formation of salts depends on the equilibrium constants for the formation of these complexes. The equilibrium constants for the formation of these complexes are:
\[
\text{Mn}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{MnH}_2\text{S}_3 \quad \text{(white)}
\]
\[
\text{Na}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{NaH}_2\text{S}_3 \quad \text{(white)}
\]\[
\text{Na}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{NaH}_2\text{S}_3 \quad \text{(white)}
\]
\[
\text{Cu}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{CuH}_2\text{S}_3 \quad \text{(white)}
\]
\[
\text{Hg}^{2+} + \text{H}_O \rightleftharpoons \text{HgH}_2\text{S}_3 \quad \text{(white)}
\]

The formation constants for the salts are:
\[
\text{Mn}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{MnH}_2\text{S}_3 \quad \text{(white)}
