The difference in electronegativity (Δ) is calculated as:

Δ = O - Cl = 12.7 - 14.4 = 1.7

The electronegativity difference is 1.7. The electronegativity difference is used to determine the polarity of the bond:
- Δ < 0.0: Covalent non-bonded
- δ = 0.0 - 0.4: Covalent non-bonded
- δ = 0.4 - 0.7: Covalent non-bonded
