- \(\sin \left(\frac{11 \pi}{2} + \alpha\right) = \sin \left(5\pi + \frac{\pi}{2} + \alpha\right) = \sin \left(5\pi + \left(\frac{\pi}{2} + \alpha\right)\right) = \sin \left(\pi + \left(\pi + \frac{\pi}{2} + \alpha\right)\right) = -\sin \left(\pi + \frac{\pi}{2} + \alpha\right) = -\sin \left(\frac{3\pi}{2} + \alpha\right) = \cos \alpha\)

