To determine the differentiability of \( f(x) \) at \( x = 0 \), we compute the derivative at \( x = 0 \) using the definition of the derivative:
\[ \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{f(0 + h) - f(0)}{h} = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{f(h) - 0}{h} = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{h \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{1}{h}\right)}{h} = \lim_{h \to 0} \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{1}{h}\right). \]

