","Plasma-based astrophysical phenomena, such as solar flares and coronal mass ejections (CMEs), are characterized by the unique properties of plasma, a state of matter where the gas is ionized and charged particles (ions and electrons) are in thermal equilibrium. These properties can be observed in several ways, such as spectroscopy, X-ray observations, and other electromagnetic radiation.

